# Keep the shipped plugin bundle lean — none of this is needed at runtime.
node_modules/
__tests__/
*.test.ts
bun.lock
*.log
.DS_Store

# Contributor tooling: the repo's own dev skill (issue triage) that the agentic CI
# workflows run. Neither manifest reaches .claude/ — both declare
# "skills": "./skills/" — so this is bundle hygiene, not a correctness fix.
.claude/

# Policy and process for humans on GitHub, none of it reachable from an installed
# plugin. README.md and AGENTS.md deliberately still ship — they are what someone
# inspecting an installed copy reads — but nothing below is addressed to that
# reader, and .github/ is issue/PR templates plus the CI-only workflows, gates and
# scripts, none of which a user runs.
SECURITY.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
CHANGELOG.md
.github/
